      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "60 patients with mandibular fractures were checked up and in whom clinically and with the help of neurophysiological methods some sensori-paresthetic disorders were diagnosed. Pain syndrome expression in cases of fractures and contraindication to analgesics use in a number of patients dictate the necessity to search new treatment methods of this category of patients. The use of transcutaneous electric stimulation of nerves allowing in short periods of time to stop pain syndrome and reduce the number of complications in cases of mandibular fractures was substantiated."},
